LOVA Experiment 16 -- scope-aware generation (M16)

==============================================================================
  1. 1000 generated programs, with and without scope tracking
==============================================================================
  outcome                                pre-M16       M16
  ----------------------------------------------------------
  unbound reference (compile error)      704 70%     0  0%
  other compile error                     47  5%     1  0%
  compiles, traps at run time             93  9%   629 63%
  compiles and runs                      156 16%   370 37%
  ----------------------------------------------------------
  references emitted                        1306       122

  An unbound reference is now unrepresentable by generation, as
  Axiom 3 always said ill-typed programs were.  The compiler's
  scope pass still exists, for trees that did not come from the
  generator: hand-written, mutated, or read back from text.

==============================================================================
  2. What fills an `Fn` slot (Q54)
==============================================================================
  apply head is                  pre-M16       M16
  --------------------------------------------------
  a reference                         74         5
  a lambda / loop-until               62       110

  Before, a reference in an Fn slot named whatever the sampler
  drew -- almost never a bound function.  After, it names a bound
  function or is not offered, so the depth bias reaches for
  `lambda` instead and the program closes.

==============================================================================
  3. The boundary: what the compiler accepts that generation cannot reach
==============================================================================
  program shape                         compiles  validates
  ------------------------------------------------------------
  self recursion                            True       True
  nested lets, later sees earlier           True       True
  shadowing                                 True       True
  mutual recursion (M12 chain)              True      False

  A left-to-right machine cannot emit a reference to a name bound
  later, so a mutually recursive def chain -- legal since M12 --
  is compilable but not generatable.  The generator is strictly
  more conservative than the compiler, which is the safe direction;
  the gap is 1 shape(s) in this set, and it is Q64.

==============================================================================
  Experiment 16 -- summary
==============================================================================
  unbound references in generated programs: 704/1000 -> 0/1000
  programs that compile and run:            156/1000 -> 370/1000
  Axiom 3 now holds at the name level for generated programs;
  the compiler's scope pass remains the check for everything else.
